{
 "_comment": "Common given names that must never enter this repository (gate G24, owner-proposed 2026-08-15). Source: the US Social Security Administration top names of the last 100 years, plus the top 200 of each sex for every decade from the 1970s through the 2020s, uniques kept - the child's generation and the parents', read from ssa.gov the same day - PUBLIC registry data, so committing it names no real person. Scanned like the private denylist: whole word, case-insensitive, camel-glued identifiers included - which is what catches a common name written in lowercase, the stated blind spot of the vocabulary layer. Names that collide with this repository own language at adoption are excluded and listed below with reasons, or the gate would cry wolf on its own bank (wren is a Level 9 word, amber is a UI colour): the residue for those is the optional private list. The list can only grow; growing it is an owner-visible diff.",
 "source": "ssa.gov: decades/century.html and decades/names1970s-2020s.html, read 2026-08-15. The per-year top-1000 query engine returns an empty shell and the bulk zip is 403-walled to non-browsers - recorded so nobody retries blind; the decade union is the deepest honest read available.",
